They are adapted from the translation tables of English Wiktionary (https://en.wiktionary.org), whose
text is © its contributors and licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 and the GFDL, as extracted by Wiktextract
(https://kaikki.org). Changes: translations were selected (up to four per part of speech for the most
common English words, leaving out archaic, rare, crude and sexual senses), cleaned (notes in brackets
and Arabic script's optional vowel marks removed) and stored as SQLite.

You may share and adapt them for any purpose, including commercially, if you give appropriate credit,
link to the licence, say what was changed, and share your adaptations under the same licence.
